{"answer": "It is denied by default. `authorityOf` in `apps/api/src/oversight/toolAuthority.ts` treats a tool with no row as `requires_human_action`, so the tool never executes. Both enforcement points apply this. The lookup only matches the table's own keys, so an inherited name such as `toString` is denied too.

The gate (`withHumanOversight`) never calls the executor of a `requires_human_action` tool. It returns a constant result, `{"error":"requires_human_action","escalation":"blocked_consequential_call"}`, as a normal result and does not throw.

The spec also says that `assertAllToolsDeclared.ts` makes the api fail at startup if a registered tool has no declared authority. This is a spec requirement (FR-004). I did not check the implementation, only the spec text.", "sources": ["specs/support-agent-human-oversight/spec.md (FR-003, FR-004)", "docs/human-oversight.md", "pull-280", "issue-448", "issue-445"]}

